WEBVTT

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.680
Ensign Kim,
please try and hold us steady.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.810
This material is extremely

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:20.875
fragile.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.115
Sorry, Doc,
I'm doing the best I can.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.417
Maybe I should've insisted

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:27.949
on a more experienced pilot,
like Mr. Paris.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.959
Oh, I'd give anything
to trade places with him

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:30.961
right now.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.055
Seven, can you join me, please?

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.259
On my way.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.266
I don't know

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.529
if I can take
three more days

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.729
of chasing comets with him.

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.362
The time might
pass more easily

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.839
if we disable
his vocal processor.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:50.215
I thought you might
find this interesting.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.147
Pre-animate biomatter.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.783
Look deeper.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:05.327
An undeveloped nucleus contained
in a cytoplasmic matrix.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.662
And buried deep inside
that nucleus...

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.931
primitive strands of DNA.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.902
The beginnings of life, Seven.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.530
What's your point?

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:17.098
When I look at this,
I don't see a mere cell.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.940
I see the potential
for literature

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.671
and art, empires

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:21.679
and kingdoms.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.340
Perhaps your visual subroutines

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.440
are malfunctioning.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:28.077
Someday...

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.679
this cytoplasmic
matrix may fall

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.123
into the primordial sea
of a distant world,

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:35.855
where it could ignite
an evolutionary process.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.056
Eons from now,
a creature not unlike you

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.964
could emerge, look
up at the stars

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.365
and ask, "Who am I?

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.666
How did I come to be?"

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:49.174
It's the miracle of creation,
Seven.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.039
Doesn't that excite you?

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.278
Ensign Kim, I asked you
to hold us steady.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.451
We're under attack!

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.633
This is the Federation Ship
Delta Flyer.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:55.963
We're on a peaceful mission.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.297
Hold your fire.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.964
You're transporting
a suspected photonic insurgent

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.006
through Lokirrim space.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.667
Drop your shields
and prepare to be boarded.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.735
Photonic insurgent?

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.644
L-if you're referring
to the hologram,

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:10.706
he's our Doctor.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.646
Seven, we've lost thrusters.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.314
I'll try reinitializing
the driver coils.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.653
Voyager, this is the Flyer.
Mayday!

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:19.657
Come in.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.057
Subspace communications

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:22.560
are off-line.

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.929
It's a tractor beam.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.397
Remodulate our shields.

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.662
That should break us free.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.801
Shields are down.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.835
What's happening?

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:42.710
They're using
some kind of disruption field.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.579
It's decompiling your matrix.

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:45.879
Federation vessel.

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.283
Power down your systems

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.911
and prepare to surrender
the photonic.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.182
Seven, they're pulling us in.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.349
You're going to have to hide
the Doctor's program.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.825
Do something, please.

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:00.257
We don't want to hurt you.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.732
We're here for the insurgent.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.463
Where's the photonic?

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.700
You decompiled his matrix.

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:10.174
You murdered him.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.608
Seven?

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:14.408
I'm sorry.
There wasn't enough time.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.174
Biogenic material.

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.686
It could be used
to create viral weapons.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.119
Confiscate it.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.781
Our Doctor was using
these spores

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.690
to synthesize new
medicines, not weapons.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.125
What's this?

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:35.023
It's my portable
regeneration unit.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.659
I have a unique physiology.

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:37.862
This device

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.701
maintains my cybernetic systems.

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:42.035
Have this analyzed.

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:43.200
Yes, sir.

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.437
There's no one else aboard.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.944
Take them to detention,

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:49.573
and secure their ship
in the Docking Bay.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.708
You got what you wanted.
Let us go.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.081
Transporting photonics

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:56.610
and manufacturing biogenic
weapons are serious charges.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.053
Let's go.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.869
I want to talk
to your superior!

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:17.910
Careful, Ensign,

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:19.740
or you'll fracture
a metacarpal.

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.837
That'd be the least
of our problems.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:25.611
The situation is not as
desperate as it appears.

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:27.710
Not as desperate?

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:30.119
We're prisoners
on an alien ship.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:31.850
Voyager has no idea
we're missing,

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:34.620
and the Doctor's
been decompiled.

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:39.256
The reports of my decompilation
have been greatly exaggerated.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:43.126
Doc?

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.937
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:50.168
Seven downloaded my program

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:52.268
into her cybernetic matrix.

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:54.870
An interesting sensation,
to say the least.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:57.108
And now you're in control
of Seven's body?

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:59.310
Total control, it seems.

00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:00.317
What about Seven?

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:01.478
Is she all right?

00:07:01.554 --> 00:07:04.079
I scanned her before the aliens
came aboard.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:05.852
Physiologically, she's fine.

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:07.256
As for her consciousness,

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.884
I'm assuming it's submerged,

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.622
but there's no way to be sure,

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:13.460
until I vacate her systems
and conduct a neurological exam.

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:14.500
Then we need

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:15.625
the mobile emitter.

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:16.895
This experience will make

00:07:17.003 --> 00:07:18.061
a fascinating article

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:20.196
for the Starfleet
Medical Journal.

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:21.467
Ow.

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:23.065
Careful. That's not your body,

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:25.007
remember?

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.807
I knew Seven's senses were more
acute than the average humanoid

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.847
but...

00:07:28.915 --> 00:07:30.906
I had no idea.

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:32.712
What is that?

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:33.843
What?

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.410
That smell.

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:38.749
I don't smell anything.

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:40.793
Could be an airborne toxin.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.589
Do you think
they're trying to poison us?

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:52.367
It's you.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.768
It's been a busy day.

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:58.174
I guess I'm
perspiring a little.

00:07:58.244 --> 00:08:00.303
A little?

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:04.272
Seven's had a busy day, too,
and she's come through it

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.318
smelling like
the proverbial rose.

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:15.894
Captain's Log,
Stardate 54238.3.

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:18.053
We've completed
our maintenance layover

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.620
at the Maldorian Station,

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:21.496
and we're on our way
to rendezvous

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:22.693
with the Delta Flyer.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:25.635
We expect to reach them
in 48 hours.

00:08:25.705 --> 00:08:28.071
Headache, fever,

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.803
respiratory distress, tremors.

00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:34.540
Looks like some kind of virus.

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:37.174
It is not a virus.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.512
You want to tell me

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:39.676
what's going on?

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:41.185
In the Doctor's database,

00:08:41.254 --> 00:08:46.157
you'll find a medication
under file Theta-12-Alpha.

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:47.886
Please replicate
it immediately.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.427
You know I can't

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:52.589
give out medicine
without knowing what it's for.

00:08:52.665 --> 00:08:54.428
If you must know,

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:58.596
I am suffering
from a neurochemical imbalance.

00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:00.730
An "imbalance"?

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:03.070
It is native to my species.

00:09:03.142 --> 00:09:06.509
Oh... this wouldn't be
the kind of imbalance

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:09.742
that comes around
once every seven years?

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:15.182
My Pon farr is
in the early stages.

00:09:15.254 --> 00:09:18.314
The urges are
still controllable.

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:20.655
You never fail
to amaze me, Tuvok.

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:22.626
A man of your advanced years

00:09:22.695 --> 00:09:25.129
still driven
by the mating instinct?

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:30.829
Unlike in humans, the Vulcan
libido increases with time.

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:33.235
Well, I guess there has to be
some kind of reward

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:34.830
for all that Vulcan discipline.

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:39.139
The Doctor anticipated my needs
and developed a treatment.

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.906
Combined with meditation,

00:09:41.047 --> 00:09:44.107
it will enable me
to control the symptoms.

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:46.117
Well, if that doesn't work,

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:47.846
there's always
a cold sonic shower.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.582
I'll tell the Captain
that you'll be out of commission

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:51.918
for a couple of days.

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:55.290
She will want to know why.

00:09:56.996 --> 00:09:58.930
Well, according to my tricorder,

00:09:58.998 --> 00:10:00.124
all we've got here

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:03.600
is a mild case of
the Tarkalean flu.

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:06.968
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:18.783
Mmm! I had no idea
that eating was such a...

00:10:18.851 --> 00:10:19.943
sensual experience.

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:21.953
The tastes, the textures,

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:24.785
feeling it slide down
Seven's esophagus.

00:10:24.857 --> 00:10:25.949
It's... it's exquisite!

00:10:26.025 --> 00:10:27.959
They're prison rations.

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:29.961
My uniform
probably tastes better.

00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:31.563
You know,
I was thinking.

00:10:31.631 --> 00:10:33.929
When we get back to Voyager,
perhaps you and Seven

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.968
could help me modify
my physical parameters.

00:10:36.102 --> 00:10:36.966
Why?

00:10:37.103 --> 00:10:38.331
So I can eat, of course,

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:39.837
like any other member
of the crew.

00:10:39.905 --> 00:10:41.372
There's just
one small problem...

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.634
you don't have a stomach.

00:10:42.708 --> 00:10:44.141
Where is the food
gonna go?

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:46.678
I believe we can construct
a holographic stomach.

00:10:46.746 --> 00:10:49.180
It can store the food
for eventual recycling.

00:10:49.248 --> 00:10:52.308
Eh... maybe we should focus
on something more productive,

00:10:52.385 --> 00:10:53.784
like getting out of here.

00:10:53.853 --> 00:10:55.946
Relax, Ensign.

00:10:56.022 --> 00:10:58.718
Our shipmates have never
let us down before.

00:10:58.791 --> 00:11:00.725
I'm sure the Captain
will clear up

00:11:00.793 --> 00:11:02.761
this little
misunderstanding.

00:11:02.828 --> 00:11:06.286
In the meantime,
are you going to finish that?

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:12.297
You!

00:11:12.371 --> 00:11:14.305
Come with us.

00:11:14.373 --> 00:11:15.499
I'm the senior officer.

00:11:15.574 --> 00:11:17.439
If you're going
to take someone, take me.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.102
My orders were specific.

00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:20.611
Don't worry, Ensign.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.807
I can take care of myself.

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:28.319
Mmm. My compliments
to the chef.

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:43.968
The prisoner, sir.

00:11:44.036 --> 00:11:49.167
Pulse-phased weapons,
duranium-enforced hull. Hmm.

00:11:49.241 --> 00:11:52.335
Much more sophisticated than
the typical smuggler's vessel.

00:11:52.411 --> 00:11:54.971
How many ways do you
want me to say this?

00:11:55.081 --> 00:11:57.845
We are not smugglers
or terrorists.

00:11:57.917 --> 00:11:59.350
We are explorers.

00:11:59.418 --> 00:12:00.976
Let us contact our ship.

00:12:01.053 --> 00:12:02.816
Our Captain will
explain everything.

00:12:02.888 --> 00:12:05.254
If you're innocent,
then you won't mind

00:12:05.324 --> 00:12:07.383
telling me more
about this vessel.

00:12:08.427 --> 00:12:11.863
For instance, um...
this device.

00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:14.126
What does it do?

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:16.430
That's a standard
food replicator.

00:12:16.502 --> 00:12:18.470
Can it be used to
create bioweapons?

00:12:18.537 --> 00:12:23.372
Not unless you count
Mr. Neelix's Bolian soufflé.

00:12:23.442 --> 00:12:25.171
Let me show you.

00:12:25.244 --> 00:12:29.305
Computer, one slice
of New York cheesecake.

00:12:32.518 --> 00:12:34.281
This is an old Earth delicacy.

00:12:34.353 --> 00:12:37.117
How do I know you're not trying
to poison me?

00:12:37.189 --> 00:12:40.556
Oh, please.

00:12:44.697 --> 00:12:47.131
Mmm...

00:12:48.434 --> 00:12:50.698
Mmm!

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.294
Oh...

00:12:52.371 --> 00:12:55.169
Oh, I never imagined... Mmm!

00:12:55.241 --> 00:12:56.970
Is this the first time
you've tried that?

00:12:58.644 --> 00:13:02.580
Of course not,
but it's just that I usually...

00:13:02.648 --> 00:13:06.914
avoid foods
that are this... rich.

00:13:06.986 --> 00:13:08.647
I do have a figure to maintain.

00:13:08.721 --> 00:13:11.246
Oh, I better get
another for you.

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:15.623
Uh, computer, another
slice of cheesecake.

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:19.464
Uh... here.

00:13:27.673 --> 00:13:30.437
Mmm.

00:13:30.509 --> 00:13:33.672
What other foods
can that device create?

00:13:35.347 --> 00:13:37.577
Hmm...

00:13:41.687 --> 00:13:45.054
Oh... during my time
with the collective,

00:13:45.124 --> 00:13:47.752
we assimilated
thousands of cultures

00:13:47.827 --> 00:13:50.762
from one end of the galaxy
to the other.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:54.664
I'll say this for the Borg,
we certainly do travel.

00:13:56.001 --> 00:13:58.561
Oh, of course, my life
didn't truly begin

00:13:58.637 --> 00:14:00.730
until I came aboard Voyager

00:14:00.806 --> 00:14:04.572
and met the person who...
who changed my life,

00:14:04.643 --> 00:14:07.737
the only one who
truly believed in me,

00:14:07.813 --> 00:14:09.576
saw my true potential...

00:14:09.648 --> 00:14:10.910
Your Captain?

00:14:10.983 --> 00:14:12.917
Our Doctor.

00:14:12.985 --> 00:14:16.580
That's right, the "photonic."

00:14:16.655 --> 00:14:19.453
If only you could
have known him.

00:14:19.525 --> 00:14:24.485
Ruggedly handsome, a sharp wit,
a towering intellect...

00:14:24.563 --> 00:14:28.294
If he and I hadn't been
colleagues, well...

00:14:28.367 --> 00:14:30.301
Now we'll never know

00:14:30.369 --> 00:14:32.860
what heights
he could have reached.

00:14:32.938 --> 00:14:35.338
I hope you understand,
I had no choice.

00:14:35.407 --> 00:14:37.136
"I was just following orders."

00:14:37.209 --> 00:14:38.471
I've heard that before.

00:14:38.544 --> 00:14:41.445
Maybe there's something
I could do for you.

00:14:41.513 --> 00:14:43.640
Uh, I-I'll speak
to my superiors...

00:14:43.716 --> 00:14:44.876
ask for leniency.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:48.681
Hmm. If I survive that long.

00:14:48.754 --> 00:14:49.948
What do you mean?

00:14:50.022 --> 00:14:53.685
My cybernetic components
are already depolarizing.

00:14:53.759 --> 00:14:56.694
I need my regener...
regeneration device.

00:14:56.762 --> 00:14:58.389
As you can see,

00:14:58.464 --> 00:15:02.525
my motor functions
are already impaired.

00:15:03.969 --> 00:15:05.561
Right.

00:15:05.638 --> 00:15:10.405
If I give this... back to you,

00:15:10.476 --> 00:15:12.876
will you do something for me?

00:15:17.149 --> 00:15:19.913
It was so nice of you
to escort me.

00:15:19.985 --> 00:15:22.579
Ah, nice to see you, Ensign.

00:15:22.655 --> 00:15:23.917
Are you drunk?

00:15:23.989 --> 00:15:25.081
It wasn't my fault.

00:15:25.157 --> 00:15:27.182
Seven's unique
physiology is... unique.

00:15:27.259 --> 00:15:29.090
It doesn't react well
to synthehol.

00:15:29.161 --> 00:15:30.651
What happened?

00:15:30.729 --> 00:15:32.822
Captain Ranek and I shared
a meal aboard the Flyer.

00:15:32.898 --> 00:15:35.025
He's really a gentleman
once you get to know him.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.761
You had a dinner date
in Seven's body?

00:15:36.835 --> 00:15:38.097
It wasn't a "date."

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.933
It was a tactical maneuver,

00:15:40.005 --> 00:15:42.599
designed to win the trust
of our captors,

00:15:42.675 --> 00:15:45.109
and it worked.

00:15:45.177 --> 00:15:46.610
I won't ask what you
had to do to get this.

00:15:46.679 --> 00:15:48.476
Nothing unladylike,
I assure you.

00:15:48.547 --> 00:15:50.913
They lost their medic
in a recent skirmish,

00:15:50.983 --> 00:15:52.746
and I offered
to take his place.

00:15:52.818 --> 00:15:54.217
Let's download your program

00:15:54.286 --> 00:15:55.947
before they change their mind.

00:15:59.959 --> 00:16:02.052
Hey, careful where you point
those tubules.

00:16:02.127 --> 00:16:04.459
Sorry.

00:16:12.137 --> 00:16:13.263
Easy.

00:16:13.339 --> 00:16:14.897
How do you feel?

00:16:14.974 --> 00:16:17.568
I'm impaired.

00:16:17.643 --> 00:16:19.201
You've had quite a shock
to your system.

00:16:19.278 --> 00:16:20.506
Let me explain what's happened.

00:16:20.579 --> 00:16:22.240
I know exactly
what's happened.

00:16:22.314 --> 00:16:24.179
You've been abusing my body.

00:16:31.056 --> 00:16:32.387
- I'm a doctor!
- Shh!

00:16:32.458 --> 00:16:34.926
I would never
abuse your body.

00:16:34.994 --> 00:16:37.292
I was trying to
get information.

00:16:37.363 --> 00:16:39.888
Sometimes a, a glass
of wine can...

00:16:39.965 --> 00:16:41.193
Ioosen the tongue.

00:16:41.266 --> 00:16:42.460
One glass.

00:16:42.534 --> 00:16:44.434
That doesn't excuse
the other eight.

00:16:44.503 --> 00:16:45.629
Was it that many?

00:16:46.772 --> 00:16:48.296
Seven, you were aware

00:16:48.374 --> 00:16:49.773
of everything?

00:16:49.842 --> 00:16:51.104
Painfully.

00:16:51.176 --> 00:16:52.575
I'm afraid the role

00:16:52.644 --> 00:16:55.204
of "spy" wasn't written
into my program.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.111
I was forced to...
improvise.

00:16:57.182 --> 00:17:00.845
You "improvised" your way
through an entire cheesecake,

00:17:00.919 --> 00:17:04.514
as well as three servings
of Ktarian chocolate puffs.

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:07.150
Now I have to suffer
the consequences.

00:17:07.226 --> 00:17:09.786
I apologize if I...
overindulged.

00:17:09.862 --> 00:17:12.296
I'll be more careful next time.

00:17:12.364 --> 00:17:13.888
There won't be a next time.

00:17:14.033 --> 00:17:15.295
I'll be discovered.

00:17:15.367 --> 00:17:16.891
They'll decompile my program.

00:17:17.002 --> 00:17:18.731
Shh!

00:17:22.007 --> 00:17:23.770
I know this is
difficult for you,

00:17:23.842 --> 00:17:26.072
but you're going to
have put up with it,

00:17:26.145 --> 00:17:27.908
until we can get
out of here.

00:17:28.047 --> 00:17:29.912
How do you propose
we do that?

00:17:29.982 --> 00:17:32.576
Maybe you can tap
into their com system,

00:17:32.651 --> 00:17:33.913
get a message to Voyager.

00:17:34.053 --> 00:17:36.920
Deciphering alien computers
isn't exactly my forte.

00:17:36.989 --> 00:17:38.047
But it is one of mine.

00:17:38.123 --> 00:17:39.454
If you can get close enough

00:17:39.525 --> 00:17:41.356
while they're accessing
their systems,

00:17:41.427 --> 00:17:43.418
I'll be able to observe
their command protocols.

00:17:43.495 --> 00:17:44.826
What's the situation?

00:17:44.897 --> 00:17:45.864
The Captain wants
the female

00:17:45.931 --> 00:17:47.592
prisoner in
the Medical Bay.

00:17:47.666 --> 00:17:49.861
We should proceed.

00:17:53.872 --> 00:17:55.305
You're saving my life.

00:17:55.374 --> 00:17:57.865
I want you to know
how grateful I am.

00:17:57.943 --> 00:17:59.410
Try to remember that

00:17:59.478 --> 00:18:02.811
the next time you're tempted
to overindulge.

00:18:16.061 --> 00:18:19.189
Photonics' viral weapon
attacks the cerebral cortex.

00:18:19.264 --> 00:18:21.198
Within days,
the victims suffer

00:18:21.266 --> 00:18:22.790
complete synaptic failure.

00:18:22.868 --> 00:18:24.631
Well, if we can't stop
the virus,

00:18:24.703 --> 00:18:26.728
we may be able to slow
its progress.

00:18:26.805 --> 00:18:29.171
We need to synthesize
a neural inhibitor.

00:18:32.678 --> 00:18:35.613
Forgive me, but aren't you
the ship's Tactical Officer?

00:18:35.681 --> 00:18:38.149
Tactical Officer,
Medic, Engineer.

00:18:38.217 --> 00:18:41.118
We've lost nearly a third
of our crew to the photonics.

00:18:41.186 --> 00:18:43.654
Well, you certainly know
your way around a medical bay.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:46.248
You may have missed
your true calling.

00:18:46.325 --> 00:18:48.793
Actually, Emmik always thought
I'd become a teacher.

00:18:48.861 --> 00:18:50.852
He used to call me
"the little professor."

00:18:50.929 --> 00:18:52.590
Who's Emmik?

00:18:52.664 --> 00:18:55.428
The photonic who helped
raise my brother and me.

00:18:55.501 --> 00:18:58.299
He knew more about treating
scrapes and bruises

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:00.429
than any organic doctor
I ever met.

00:19:00.506 --> 00:19:02.531
Sounds like someone
I'd enjoy meeting.

00:19:02.608 --> 00:19:05.202
Maybe...
before he joined the insurgency.

00:19:05.277 --> 00:19:07.404
Why did he do that?

00:19:07.479 --> 00:19:10.710
I ask myself that question
every day.

00:19:10.782 --> 00:19:14.718
We never treated him
like a servant,

00:19:14.786 --> 00:19:16.617
but he turned against us anyway.

00:19:16.688 --> 00:19:24.094
Is it... possible he felt...
subjugated?

00:19:24.163 --> 00:19:25.892
I don't see how.

00:19:25.964 --> 00:19:28.592
He lived his own life,
pursued his own interests.

00:19:28.667 --> 00:19:31.101
He was part of our family.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:34.105
At least I thought he was.

00:19:34.173 --> 00:19:36.801
We should get back
to the patient.

00:19:42.014 --> 00:19:43.914
It could take up
to a day to determine

00:19:44.049 --> 00:19:45.516
if the inhibitor
is working.

00:19:45.584 --> 00:19:46.915
Thank you.

00:19:47.019 --> 00:19:49.453
Don't thank me.
Thank my ship's doctor.

00:19:49.521 --> 00:19:52.422
He taught me everything
I know about medicine

00:19:52.491 --> 00:19:53.480
and remember...

00:19:53.559 --> 00:19:54.856
he was a photonic.

00:19:54.927 --> 00:19:56.451
Actually, you have a lot

00:19:56.528 --> 00:19:57.722
in common with him.

00:19:57.796 --> 00:20:00.788
He was something
of a jack-of-all-trades, too.

00:20:00.866 --> 00:20:02.527
I suspect you'd
have gotten along

00:20:02.601 --> 00:20:04.125
famously.

00:20:04.203 --> 00:20:08.037
I'm certain he would've taken
a liking to you.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.287
Your neurotransmitters

00:20:22.354 --> 00:20:23.685
aren't absorbing
the medication.

00:20:23.755 --> 00:20:25.382
Can you increase
the dosage?

00:20:25.457 --> 00:20:27.823
Not without causing damage
to your neocortex.

00:20:27.893 --> 00:20:29.292
The Doc might be able
to synthesize

00:20:29.361 --> 00:20:30.350
a stronger medicine, but...

00:20:30.429 --> 00:20:31.623
I'll make the best

00:20:31.697 --> 00:20:34.063
of the situation
until he returns.

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.474
I do have one area
of expertise

00:20:43.542 --> 00:20:44.873
that might help...

00:20:44.943 --> 00:20:47.571
the holodeck.

00:20:47.646 --> 00:20:50.308
I am a married man.

00:20:50.382 --> 00:20:52.475
Look, it's the
holodeck, Tuvok;

00:20:52.551 --> 00:20:54.075
it doesn't count.

00:20:54.152 --> 00:20:56.518
Is that what you tell
your wife?

00:20:56.588 --> 00:20:58.988
No, of course not.

00:20:59.124 --> 00:21:01.183
My days of rescuing
slave girls

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:03.125
from Planet 10 are history.

00:21:03.195 --> 00:21:06.926
Look, you have photographs
of your wife, right?

00:21:07.065 --> 00:21:08.828
Well, the computer
can use them

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:10.060
to create a replica.

00:21:10.135 --> 00:21:11.932
It wouldn't be
breaking your vows

00:21:12.037 --> 00:21:13.937
if it's a hologram
of your wife.

00:21:20.846 --> 00:21:22.609
As it was in the dawn
of our days,

00:21:22.681 --> 00:21:25.479
as it will be
for all tomorrows,

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:28.815
to you, my husband, I
consecrate all that I am.

00:21:28.887 --> 00:21:29.945
T'Pel, my wife,

00:21:30.088 --> 00:21:32.852
from you I receive
all that I am.

00:21:32.924 --> 00:21:36.883
As it was in the beginning,
so shall it be now.

00:21:36.962 --> 00:21:40.090
Two bodies; one mind.

00:21:44.436 --> 00:21:47.735
I'm picking up a vessel
closing at high impulse.

00:21:47.806 --> 00:21:50.070
They're firing.

00:21:50.142 --> 00:21:51.939
Shields are holding.

00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:52.977
Open a channel.

00:21:53.111 --> 00:21:55.511
This is Captain
Kathryn Janeway

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.775
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:21:57.849 --> 00:21:59.680
We're on a peaceful mission.

00:21:59.751 --> 00:22:01.446
We've detected photonic activity
aboard your vessel.

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:03.078
Drop your shields and prepare
to be boarded.

00:22:03.155 --> 00:22:05.282
Photonic activity?

00:22:05.357 --> 00:22:08.224
Tuvok... he's in Holodeck 2.

00:22:08.293 --> 00:22:09.453
They're firing again.

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:17.434
It's some kind
of photonic disrupter

00:22:17.502 --> 00:22:18.901
directed at Holodeck 2.

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:22.599
Target their weapons array
and fire.

00:22:27.412 --> 00:22:28.344
They're hailing.

00:22:28.413 --> 00:22:30.108
On screen.

00:22:30.182 --> 00:22:32.082
Drop your shields and prepare
to receive our inspection teams.

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:34.812
You're not in a position
to be making demands.

00:22:34.886 --> 00:22:36.251
Why did you fire on us?

00:22:36.321 --> 00:22:38.482
Your vessel is carrying
photonics

00:22:38.557 --> 00:22:39.819
through Lokirrim space.

00:22:39.891 --> 00:22:42.325
We didn't realize
that was forbidden.

00:22:42.394 --> 00:22:45.591
We'd be happy
to shut down our holodecks.

00:22:52.337 --> 00:22:55.135
Your sensors should confirm
they've been deactivated.

00:22:55.207 --> 00:22:58.904
You're still required
to submit to inspection.

00:22:58.977 --> 00:23:00.808
Your sensors should also confirm

00:23:00.879 --> 00:23:02.813
that our weapons
are ready to fire.

00:23:02.881 --> 00:23:05.247
We're both reasonable people.

00:23:05.317 --> 00:23:06.716
I suggest a compromise.

00:23:06.785 --> 00:23:10.152
Your vessel will escort us
through Lokirrim territory.

00:23:10.222 --> 00:23:12.349
That way,
you can keep an eye on us,

00:23:12.424 --> 00:23:15.154
make sure we don't reactivate
our holodecks.

00:23:15.227 --> 00:23:16.922
The other alternative is...

00:23:16.995 --> 00:23:19.293
we destroy your ship.

00:23:22.601 --> 00:23:24.933
Your proposal is acceptable.

00:23:28.173 --> 00:23:31.404
Sometimes diplomacy requires
a little saber rattling.

00:23:31.476 --> 00:23:35.173
Begin long-range scans.

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:40.647
I can picture them now...

00:23:40.719 --> 00:23:42.949
my father in
his airponics bay

00:23:43.054 --> 00:23:44.885
pruning his cona vines,

00:23:44.956 --> 00:23:48.050
my mother reading
in her favorite chair.

00:23:48.126 --> 00:23:50.788
Nothing in that home
ever changes.

00:23:50.862 --> 00:23:53.194
It must be comforting
to have a place like that

00:23:53.265 --> 00:23:54.698
to go back to.

00:23:54.766 --> 00:23:56.825
I've never been away
this long before.

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:00.930
His progress is remarkable.

00:24:01.006 --> 00:24:04.305
I want you to know,
I'm going to tell my superiors

00:24:04.376 --> 00:24:06.241
everything
you've done for us.

00:24:06.311 --> 00:24:08.108
First Ranek and now you.

00:24:08.180 --> 00:24:10.478
I may become
the first prisoner of war

00:24:10.549 --> 00:24:12.483
to be decorated by his captors.

00:24:12.551 --> 00:24:17.250
I know someone
who'd really enjoy meeting you.

00:24:17.322 --> 00:24:19.552
Who?

00:24:19.624 --> 00:24:23.355
My brother, Lohden.

00:24:23.428 --> 00:24:24.725
Your brother?

00:24:24.796 --> 00:24:26.593
You'd like him.

00:24:26.665 --> 00:24:28.428
He's ambitious, accomplished,

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:30.695
and he'd love
your sense of humor.

00:24:30.769 --> 00:24:33.203
Hmm. Apparently, it's my

00:24:33.271 --> 00:24:35.205
most attractive quality.

00:24:35.273 --> 00:24:37.207
Seven of Nine.

00:24:37.275 --> 00:24:39.869
Please report to the Bridge.

00:24:52.224 --> 00:24:54.954
Let me guess... your crew
decided to abandon ship.

00:24:55.093 --> 00:24:57.357
I wanted to thank you.

00:24:57.429 --> 00:24:59.454
I had a wonderful time
the other night.

00:24:59.531 --> 00:25:02.659
It's not often that I...

00:25:02.734 --> 00:25:04.668
indulge myself like that.

00:25:04.736 --> 00:25:06.499
It's been a long time
for me, too.

00:25:06.571 --> 00:25:09.472
I remembered your interest
in stellar phenomenon,

00:25:09.541 --> 00:25:11.372
so I requested
a course change

00:25:11.443 --> 00:25:13.172
to show you something.

00:25:24.055 --> 00:25:25.818
What is it?

00:25:25.891 --> 00:25:29.554
To an astronomer,
it's simply a pulsar cluster,

00:25:29.628 --> 00:25:32.222
but our poets call it
the "Window of Dreams."

00:25:32.297 --> 00:25:35.596
You could travel from one end
of the Quadrant to the other

00:25:35.667 --> 00:25:36.895
and never see anything like it.

00:25:36.968 --> 00:25:39.835
Lovely! Hmm.

00:25:44.109 --> 00:25:45.838
It's the pulsar's
EM fields

00:25:45.911 --> 00:25:47.606
vibrating against
our hull.

00:25:47.679 --> 00:25:49.044
Huh.

00:25:49.114 --> 00:25:52.106
I once thought this was
the most beautiful sight

00:25:52.183 --> 00:25:53.241
in the sector.

00:25:53.318 --> 00:25:54.444
Hmm.

00:25:54.519 --> 00:25:56.987
I see now that I was wrong.

00:25:58.924 --> 00:26:00.152
Hmm.

00:26:00.225 --> 00:26:02.193
Oh. I almost forgot.

00:26:02.260 --> 00:26:05.559
Oh, I promised a friend
I'd go easy on the synthehol.

00:26:07.198 --> 00:26:08.995
Do you hear that?

00:26:09.067 --> 00:26:11.228
It's identical to the rhythm
produced

00:26:11.303 --> 00:26:13.464
by the eight-chambered
Ktarian heart.

00:26:13.538 --> 00:26:15.096
Hmm.

00:26:20.178 --> 00:26:21.475
Is something wrong?

00:26:23.148 --> 00:26:24.672
Rapid pulse,
respiratory distress.

00:26:24.749 --> 00:26:27.343
You may be having a reaction
to the pulsar's radiation.

00:26:27.419 --> 00:26:30.149
We should get you
to the Medical Bay.

00:26:30.221 --> 00:26:32.485
No, I'm not going
to the Medical Bay.

00:26:32.557 --> 00:26:34.115
You starship Captains
are all alike.

00:26:34.192 --> 00:26:36.353
You can stare down the barrel
of a phaser cannon,

00:26:36.428 --> 00:26:38.419
but you can't stomach
a simple medical exam.

00:26:38.496 --> 00:26:41.522
I don't need an exam to know
what I'm suffering from.

00:26:46.805 --> 00:26:47.863
I'm sorry. I thought...

00:26:47.939 --> 00:26:48.906
You were wrong.

00:26:48.974 --> 00:26:50.236
I didn't mean to offend you.

00:26:50.308 --> 00:26:51.240
It's just...

00:26:51.309 --> 00:26:52.901
I've never met a woman
like you before.

00:26:52.978 --> 00:26:55.378
That's because there are
no women like me.

00:27:08.860 --> 00:27:10.851
Is something wrong?

00:27:10.929 --> 00:27:12.419
Ranek summoned me
to the Bridge

00:27:12.497 --> 00:27:15.193
under the pretext
of a little stargazing.

00:27:15.266 --> 00:27:17.530
What he really wanted
was to use my face

00:27:17.602 --> 00:27:18.694
as a tongue depressor.

00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:20.260
I'm surprised
to hear that.

00:27:20.338 --> 00:27:21.862
It was completely inappropriate!

00:27:21.940 --> 00:27:23.464
That kind of behavior

00:27:23.541 --> 00:27:26.271
would get a Starfleet Captain
reassigned to a garbage scow.

00:27:26.344 --> 00:27:28.005
I'm not defending
what he did, but...

00:27:28.079 --> 00:27:29.046
you have to understand

00:27:29.114 --> 00:27:30.741
we've been out here
for a long time.

00:27:30.815 --> 00:27:32.908
It's difficult to
hide your feelings,

00:27:33.018 --> 00:27:34.485
especially when
you work closely

00:27:34.552 --> 00:27:37.214
with someone you're
attracted to.

00:27:37.288 --> 00:27:41.019
You... have feelings for him?

00:27:44.029 --> 00:27:45.894
I've known Lotharios
like Ranek.

00:27:45.964 --> 00:27:48.057
Trust me, you don't
want anything to do with him.

00:27:48.133 --> 00:27:50.260
You need someone who...

00:27:50.335 --> 00:27:52.895
who can appreciate
your many talents.

00:27:52.971 --> 00:27:55.439
Someone... overflowing

00:27:55.507 --> 00:27:58.476
with intelligence
and compassion,

00:27:58.543 --> 00:27:59.635
someone capable...

00:27:59.711 --> 00:28:00.735
Ow!

00:28:02.580 --> 00:28:03.604
Ah!

00:28:03.682 --> 00:28:05.240
It looks like a spasm
in the trapezius.

00:28:05.316 --> 00:28:07.341
I had no idea
it could be...

00:28:07.419 --> 00:28:08.477
so excruciating.

00:28:08.553 --> 00:28:09.485
That's what happens

00:28:09.554 --> 00:28:11.146
when you work so long
without rest.

00:28:11.222 --> 00:28:12.280
Ah!

00:28:12.357 --> 00:28:13.289
Our last medic

00:28:13.358 --> 00:28:14.586
showed me a technique
that might help.

00:28:14.659 --> 00:28:15.591
I-I'll try it,
if you like.

00:28:15.660 --> 00:28:16.922
Please, anything!

00:28:18.630 --> 00:28:20.757
Oh, that...

00:28:20.832 --> 00:28:24.427
that feels... wonderful.

00:28:24.502 --> 00:28:25.992
Oh...

00:28:33.144 --> 00:28:34.475
Did I hurt you?

00:28:34.546 --> 00:28:35.911
No, no-no, no, no, no.

00:28:36.047 --> 00:28:37.105
Well, then what's wrong?

00:28:39.784 --> 00:28:42.252
There's something
you don't know about me,

00:28:42.320 --> 00:28:45.016
something I have to tell you.

00:28:45.090 --> 00:28:46.318
It's all right.

00:28:46.391 --> 00:28:48.552
I know.

00:28:48.626 --> 00:28:49.854
You do?

00:28:49.928 --> 00:28:51.259
How could you?

00:28:51.329 --> 00:28:54.821
Your cybernetic implants,
your portable regenerator?

00:28:54.899 --> 00:28:57.868
You're not going
to tell anyone, are you?

00:28:57.936 --> 00:29:00.700
I would never say anything
to the crew,

00:29:00.772 --> 00:29:02.672
but Ranek knows.

00:29:02.741 --> 00:29:04.333
He does?

00:29:04.409 --> 00:29:06.877
Of course, it was apparent
the moment we scanned you.

00:29:07.011 --> 00:29:09.844
I can't believe
you didn't say anything.

00:29:09.914 --> 00:29:12.212
It wouldn't have been
appropriate.

00:29:12.283 --> 00:29:14.751
You're part Borg.

00:29:14.819 --> 00:29:16.878
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:29:17.021 --> 00:29:18.420
Ah. Mmm.

00:29:18.490 --> 00:29:19.889
Security to Medical Bay.

00:29:19.991 --> 00:29:22.084
This is Lieutenant Jaryn.

00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:23.627
The prisoner is ill.

00:29:23.695 --> 00:29:26.027
He's requesting treatment
by his crewmate.

00:29:26.097 --> 00:29:27.359
Hmm.

00:29:30.301 --> 00:29:31.563
Ensign.

00:29:34.606 --> 00:29:36.369
Where the hell have you been?

00:29:36.441 --> 00:29:37.430
I had to fake a seizure

00:29:37.509 --> 00:29:39.238
before the guard would
let me see you.

00:29:39.310 --> 00:29:40.242
Calm down.

00:29:40.311 --> 00:29:42.006
Seven and I have been
making progress.

00:29:48.953 --> 00:29:50.614
Did you get a look

00:29:50.688 --> 00:29:52.121
at their computer?

00:29:52.190 --> 00:29:53.452
During the one brief moment

00:29:53.525 --> 00:29:55.550
when the Doctor wasn't
indulging himself.

00:29:55.627 --> 00:29:58.152
I think I've shown
considerable restraint

00:29:58.229 --> 00:29:59.321
under the circumstances.

00:29:59.397 --> 00:30:00.921
Kissing Ranek on the Bridge?

00:30:01.065 --> 00:30:02.726
Is that your idea of restraint?

00:30:02.801 --> 00:30:03.790
Kissing?

00:30:03.868 --> 00:30:05.301
Not that it's any
of your business,

00:30:05.370 --> 00:30:06.735
but if you must know,

00:30:06.805 --> 00:30:08.102
Ranek kissed me.

00:30:08.173 --> 00:30:10.266
And the massage you got
from Lieutenant Jaryn?

00:30:10.341 --> 00:30:11.831
Entirely therapeutic.

00:30:11.910 --> 00:30:14.640
You became sexually aroused
in my body.

00:30:17.148 --> 00:30:20.174
When did it become a crime
to enjoy a sensation or two?

00:30:20.251 --> 00:30:22.776
Of course, you'd be the last
person to understand that.

00:30:22.854 --> 00:30:24.082
What do you mean?

00:30:24.155 --> 00:30:27.556
The whole world is full
of experiences and sensations,

00:30:27.625 --> 00:30:29.752
but you insist
on denying yourself.

00:30:29.828 --> 00:30:31.523
Instead of replicating caviar,

00:30:31.596 --> 00:30:33.427
you choose
nutritional supplement

00:30:33.498 --> 00:30:34.760
13-Alpha.

00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:35.959
Caviar is an indulgence.

00:30:36.067 --> 00:30:37.796
Indulgences are what
make life worth living!

00:30:37.869 --> 00:30:39.700
Shh!

00:30:39.771 --> 00:30:42.604
These last few days
have been a revelation.

00:30:42.674 --> 00:30:44.801
Feeling your lungs
fill with air,

00:30:44.876 --> 00:30:46.901
the surge of adrenaline
through your veins.

00:30:46.978 --> 00:30:48.309
Until I spent a day
in your skin,

00:30:48.379 --> 00:30:49.778
I never knew what I was missing.

00:30:49.848 --> 00:30:52.373
You may have been
better off not knowing.

00:30:52.450 --> 00:30:54.281
We're quite a pair.

00:30:54.352 --> 00:30:57.116
Me, trapped by the limitations
of photons and force fields.

00:30:57.188 --> 00:31:00.453
You, by a drone's obsession
with efficiency.

00:31:00.525 --> 00:31:02.652
You'd make an excellent
hologram.

00:31:02.727 --> 00:31:03.523
All right!

00:31:03.595 --> 00:31:04.789
Listen, you can argue

00:31:04.863 --> 00:31:06.728
all you want when we
get back to Voyager,

00:31:06.798 --> 00:31:08.288
but that's not going to happen

00:31:08.366 --> 00:31:10.095
unless we come up with a plan.

00:31:10.168 --> 00:31:12.033
Did you learn anything
about their com system?

00:31:12.103 --> 00:31:13.661
It can only be accessed
from the Bridge,

00:31:13.738 --> 00:31:15.672
but I saw Ranek
enter his command codes.

00:31:15.740 --> 00:31:17.298
If we can get
those codes to Voyager,

00:31:17.375 --> 00:31:19.206
they may be able
to disable the shields

00:31:19.277 --> 00:31:20.574
and beam us out.

00:31:20.645 --> 00:31:22.704
How are we going to do that?

00:31:24.215 --> 00:31:26.649
The subspace
transceiver on the Flyer.

00:31:26.718 --> 00:31:27.810
Can you get aboard?

00:31:27.886 --> 00:31:29.080
It's heavily guarded.

00:31:29.153 --> 00:31:32.316
I can get us aboard.

00:31:37.028 --> 00:31:40.361
Captain, may I speak with you?

00:31:40.431 --> 00:31:41.625
Privately.

00:31:46.738 --> 00:31:48.262
I owe you an apology.

00:31:48.339 --> 00:31:50.273
Well, I was the one
who acted inappropriately.

00:31:50.341 --> 00:31:52.969
Oh, a kiss is hardly
a court-martial offense.

00:31:53.044 --> 00:31:55.171
It's just that you...
caught me by surprise.

00:31:55.246 --> 00:31:57.180
I-I won't make that
mistake again.

00:31:57.248 --> 00:31:59.808
Perhaps, we should...
start over.

00:31:59.884 --> 00:32:01.818
What did you have in mind?

00:32:01.886 --> 00:32:03.649
Oh, we could start
with a toast.

00:32:03.721 --> 00:32:05.188
I thought synth...

00:32:05.256 --> 00:32:06.689
Oh, I can make an exception

00:32:06.758 --> 00:32:09.784
for a... special occasion.

00:32:09.861 --> 00:32:13.058
Computer, champagne,
two glasses.

00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:24.370
To new beginnings.

00:32:24.442 --> 00:32:28.208
Maybe there's some
hope for us yet.

00:32:28.279 --> 00:32:32.739
As I've discovered recently,
anything is possible.

00:32:37.689 --> 00:32:39.179
Computer, dim the lights.

00:32:39.257 --> 00:32:41.452
Play EMH
Music File

00:32:41.526 --> 00:32:43.494
Gamma-12.

00:32:58.509 --> 00:32:59.441
Oh...

00:32:59.510 --> 00:33:00.670
this is interesting.

00:33:00.745 --> 00:33:01.803
It's called a waltz.

00:33:01.879 --> 00:33:04.712
Something else I learned
from our Doctor.

00:33:04.782 --> 00:33:07.649
Captain Ranek,
please come to the Bridge.

00:33:07.719 --> 00:33:09.050
What is it?

00:33:09.120 --> 00:33:10.747
We've received
an encrypted transmission.

00:33:10.822 --> 00:33:12.312
Oh, I'll be right there.

00:33:12.390 --> 00:33:14.915
You're not leaving?

00:33:14.993 --> 00:33:17.086
Um...

00:33:17.161 --> 00:33:19.789
I'll be back
as soon as I can.

00:33:19.864 --> 00:33:23.231
I really think
you should stay.

00:33:31.409 --> 00:33:34.139
Never play hard to get
with a hologram.

00:33:40.451 --> 00:33:42.078
Still no sign

00:33:42.153 --> 00:33:43.518
of the Flyer's warp signature.

00:33:43.588 --> 00:33:47.524
I appreciate your
sense of duty, Tuvok,

00:33:47.592 --> 00:33:50.060
but we can handle the
situation without you.

00:33:50.128 --> 00:33:52.494
Under the circumstances,
abandoning my post

00:33:52.563 --> 00:33:54.588
would be a dereliction
of duty.

00:33:54.665 --> 00:33:57.065
My illness is still
in the early stages.

00:33:57.135 --> 00:33:58.602
I can control it.

00:33:58.669 --> 00:34:02.400
If I remember correctly,
the last time you came down

00:34:02.473 --> 00:34:05.533
with the Tarkalean flu
was seven years ago.

00:34:05.610 --> 00:34:06.907
As soon as this is over,

00:34:07.011 --> 00:34:09.002
the holodeck
is at your disposal.

00:34:09.080 --> 00:34:12.572
There you are, Commander.

00:34:12.650 --> 00:34:14.618
Now, a person in
your condition

00:34:14.685 --> 00:34:16.346
really ought to be in bed.

00:34:16.421 --> 00:34:19.015
This is my
grandmother's recipe,

00:34:19.090 --> 00:34:21.923
guaranteed to cure even
the most stubborn flu.

00:34:22.060 --> 00:34:23.687
Now... smell that?

00:34:23.761 --> 00:34:26.195
I don't smell anything.

00:34:26.264 --> 00:34:27.595
Exactly.

00:34:27.665 --> 00:34:29.724
I prepared it just
the way you like it.

00:34:29.801 --> 00:34:32.167
No herbs or spices
of any kind.

00:34:32.236 --> 00:34:33.601
It's practically tasteless.

00:34:34.906 --> 00:34:36.806
We're receiving a hail.

00:34:36.874 --> 00:34:38.535
It's the Delta Flyer.

00:34:38.609 --> 00:34:39.541
On screen.

00:34:39.610 --> 00:34:41.407
Seven, it's good to see you.

00:34:41.479 --> 00:34:43.947
I'm afraid there's no time
for pleasantries, Captain.

00:34:44.082 --> 00:34:46.949
We're being held prisoner
on a Lokirrim patrol ship.

00:34:47.085 --> 00:34:50.054
I'm sending you our precise
location and the command codes

00:34:50.121 --> 00:34:51.452
to disable their shields.

00:34:51.522 --> 00:34:53.285
Are the Doctor and Harry
all right?

00:34:53.357 --> 00:34:56.258
Ensign Kim
is his usual chipper self.

00:34:56.327 --> 00:34:57.658
As for me, I'm looking forward

00:34:57.728 --> 00:34:59.889
to a long, uneventful shift
in Sick Bay.

00:35:03.968 --> 00:35:05.060
Doctor?

00:35:05.136 --> 00:35:07.297
It's a long story, Captain.

00:35:07.371 --> 00:35:08.804
Delta Flyer out.

00:35:08.873 --> 00:35:10.568
They may be in more
trouble than we thought.

00:35:10.641 --> 00:35:11.869
Set a course.

00:35:11.943 --> 00:35:13.137
Our escort isn't

00:35:13.211 --> 00:35:15.008
going to take
kindly to a detour.

00:35:15.079 --> 00:35:16.671
What's the status
of their weapons?

00:35:16.747 --> 00:35:19.215
They've repaired
their forward phasers.

00:35:19.283 --> 00:35:21.911
Target their power matrix.

00:35:21.986 --> 00:35:25.183
We may only get one shot,
so make it count.

00:35:26.724 --> 00:35:27.691
Ready.

00:35:27.758 --> 00:35:29.783
Do it.

00:35:32.864 --> 00:35:34.297
Direct hit.

00:35:34.365 --> 00:35:35.923
Get us out of here,
maximum warp.

00:35:45.543 --> 00:35:47.101
What's wrong with him?

00:35:47.178 --> 00:35:49.203
Apparently, Captain Ranek

00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:51.805
has an even lower tolerance
for synthehol than I do.

00:35:51.883 --> 00:35:53.475
That doesn't sound like Ranek.

00:35:53.551 --> 00:35:55.849
It's probably not something
he'd admit to his crew.

00:35:55.920 --> 00:35:58.445
We should keep this
between us.

00:36:00.958 --> 00:36:01.947
What are you doing?

00:36:02.026 --> 00:36:04.051
Reviving him.

00:36:04.128 --> 00:36:05.186
I-I wouldn't recommend that.

00:36:09.800 --> 00:36:11.791
Take her to detention.

00:36:11.869 --> 00:36:15.270
Separate her from
the other prisoner.

00:36:15.339 --> 00:36:17.466
There are traces of sedative
in your bloodstream.

00:36:19.844 --> 00:36:21.402
What was your plan?

00:36:21.479 --> 00:36:22.741
To aid the insurgents?

00:36:22.813 --> 00:36:24.246
There was no plan.

00:36:24.315 --> 00:36:25.373
We trusted you.

00:36:25.449 --> 00:36:27.417
I'm still a prisoner
on your ship,

00:36:27.485 --> 00:36:28.918
and despite our friendship,

00:36:29.053 --> 00:36:30.782
my first obligation
is to escape.

00:36:30.855 --> 00:36:32.789
We were going to
recommend leniency.

00:36:32.857 --> 00:36:34.051
If you knew who I really was,

00:36:34.125 --> 00:36:35.592
I doubt you'd be
trying to help me.

00:36:35.660 --> 00:36:39.562
Alien vessel approaching.

00:36:39.630 --> 00:36:42.030
I want her where I can see her.

00:36:52.210 --> 00:36:54.201
They are raising shields.

00:36:54.278 --> 00:36:55.711
Stand by with those
command codes.

00:36:55.780 --> 00:36:57.611
Open a channel.

00:36:57.682 --> 00:36:59.240
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:36:59.317 --> 00:37:00.784
We don't want a fight.

00:37:00.851 --> 00:37:03.115
Return my people and
we'll be on our way.

00:37:03.187 --> 00:37:04.745
Your people were caught
transporting

00:37:04.822 --> 00:37:07.484
a photonic insurgent
and biogenic material.

00:37:07.558 --> 00:37:09.526
We don't want
to disable your ship,

00:37:09.594 --> 00:37:11.118
but we will if we have to.

00:37:17.435 --> 00:37:19.426
We're losing our
ventral shield grid.

00:37:19.503 --> 00:37:20.902
Compensate.

00:37:20.972 --> 00:37:22.303
I'm trying.

00:37:22.373 --> 00:37:24.705
They've tapped into
the shield matrix.

00:37:24.775 --> 00:37:27.073
They're using your
command authorization.

00:37:31.415 --> 00:37:32.746
They're rerouting power.

00:37:32.817 --> 00:37:34.079
He's tying their shields

00:37:34.151 --> 00:37:35.812
directly into
the warp matrix.

00:37:35.886 --> 00:37:38.912
If you fire on us,
you'll trigger a core breach.

00:37:38.990 --> 00:37:41.083
You'll be killing the people
you're here to rescue.

00:37:41.158 --> 00:37:43.592
End transmission.

00:37:43.661 --> 00:37:44.889
Tractor beam.

00:37:46.897 --> 00:37:47.921
Full reverse!

00:37:47.999 --> 00:37:48.988
Target their emitters.

00:37:54.405 --> 00:37:55.565
They've broken free.

00:37:55.640 --> 00:37:57.039
Chakotay, can you send
a com signal

00:37:57.108 --> 00:37:58.507
directly to Seven's
cortical node?

00:38:02.480 --> 00:38:06.143
Doctor, if you can hear me,
we need your help.

00:38:06.217 --> 00:38:08.378
Try to disable their shields.

00:38:15.993 --> 00:38:18.018
It's a photonic.

00:38:19.363 --> 00:38:20.887
Cover me.

00:38:20.998 --> 00:38:21.896
Stay back!

00:38:21.999 --> 00:38:23.193
I'm not afraid to use this.

00:38:32.843 --> 00:38:34.003
Step away.

00:38:35.546 --> 00:38:36.911
She destabilized
the shield grid.

00:38:36.981 --> 00:38:38.073
It's failing.

00:38:39.383 --> 00:38:41.146
Watch them.

00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:51.391
If you try to
reinitialize the grid,

00:38:51.462 --> 00:38:52.429
it'll overload.

00:38:52.496 --> 00:38:54.555
We could all die.

00:38:54.632 --> 00:38:56.361
Ranek, don't!

00:39:00.004 --> 00:39:00.732
Stay back.

00:39:00.805 --> 00:39:03.273
I'm a doctor. Let me help.

00:39:03.341 --> 00:39:05.332
Their shields are down.
I have a lock.

00:39:05.409 --> 00:39:07.604
Away team, stand by
for transport.

00:39:07.678 --> 00:39:09.942
I have injured here, Captain.
I can't leave yet.

00:39:12.083 --> 00:39:13.573
He'll die

00:39:13.651 --> 00:39:14.743
without immediate surgery.

00:39:14.819 --> 00:39:16.480
I know this

00:39:16.554 --> 00:39:17.680
is difficult to grasp,

00:39:17.755 --> 00:39:19.552
but I'm the person
you've been getting to know

00:39:19.623 --> 00:39:20.612
the last few days.

00:39:20.691 --> 00:39:22.784
My program was in control
of Seven's body.

00:39:22.860 --> 00:39:24.088
You're lying.

00:39:24.161 --> 00:39:26.686
I know you have feelings
for Ranek.

00:39:27.765 --> 00:39:28.754
If he dies,

00:39:28.833 --> 00:39:31.461
you're never going
to forgive yourself.

00:39:38.609 --> 00:39:40.600
Your vital signs are stable.

00:39:42.580 --> 00:39:45.674
Suppose I should
be, uh, grateful.

00:39:45.750 --> 00:39:47.308
A "thank you" is customary

00:39:47.385 --> 00:39:49.478
after someone saves your life.

00:39:49.553 --> 00:39:54.013
What happened was between
me and Seven of Nine,

00:39:54.091 --> 00:39:55.285
not you.

00:39:55.359 --> 00:39:57.327
I'm sorry you feel that way.

00:39:57.395 --> 00:40:00.922
The truth is, aside from
a few awkward moments,

00:40:00.998 --> 00:40:04.331
I enjoyed our time together.

00:40:04.402 --> 00:40:06.666
There are many women

00:40:06.737 --> 00:40:09.297
who'd appreciate an
attractive man like you.

00:40:09.373 --> 00:40:12.035
I'm just not one of them.

00:40:12.109 --> 00:40:14.373
Um, more of our vessels
are on the way.

00:40:14.445 --> 00:40:17.642
You should leave
while you can.

00:40:17.715 --> 00:40:19.376
Thank you.

00:40:24.221 --> 00:40:25.916
I guess you won't
be introducing me

00:40:25.990 --> 00:40:27.150
to your brother.

00:40:27.224 --> 00:40:29.954
I'm not sure you're
the kind of person

00:40:30.094 --> 00:40:31.356
he's interested in.

00:40:31.429 --> 00:40:33.829
You mean because
I'm a hologram.

00:40:35.266 --> 00:40:37.700
I don't imagine this experience

00:40:37.768 --> 00:40:42.068
is going to change
your feelings about photonics.

00:40:42.139 --> 00:40:46.132
But I wanted you to know...

00:40:46.210 --> 00:40:48.804
I'm grateful for the time
we've spent together.

00:40:48.879 --> 00:40:50.972
You're a talented doctor.

00:40:51.081 --> 00:40:53.743
We're the ones
who should be grateful.

00:40:53.818 --> 00:40:55.513
I'm glad I could help.

00:40:57.288 --> 00:40:59.256
Doctor to Voyager.

00:40:59.323 --> 00:41:00.654
One to beam out.

00:41:10.434 --> 00:41:11.765
Commander...

00:41:11.836 --> 00:41:14.100
it's good to see
you're over the flu.

00:41:14.171 --> 00:41:15.229
I have fully recovered.

00:41:15.306 --> 00:41:16.637
Thank you for
your assistance.

00:41:16.707 --> 00:41:17.639
Oh, don't mention it.

00:41:17.708 --> 00:41:19.198
I just hope
everything was okay.

00:41:19.276 --> 00:41:20.766
Not exactly.

00:41:20.845 --> 00:41:23.575
My wife's ears are four
millimeters shorter

00:41:23.647 --> 00:41:24.909
than your facsimile's.

00:41:24.982 --> 00:41:26.950
So I took a little
artistic license.

00:41:27.051 --> 00:41:29.383
Aside from that,
was everything all right?

00:41:29.453 --> 00:41:32.445
The hologram was adequate,

00:41:32.523 --> 00:41:35.720
but no substitute for my wife.

00:41:35.793 --> 00:41:38.785
Of course not.

00:41:49.340 --> 00:41:51.968
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:41:52.109 --> 00:41:54.407
There isn't one... yet.

00:41:54.478 --> 00:41:57.504
The Mess Hall
is three decks up.

00:41:57.581 --> 00:41:58.946
In case you've forgotten,

00:41:59.016 --> 00:42:01.450
I've lost my appetite...
permanently.

00:42:01.519 --> 00:42:03.146
That doesn't mean
you're incapable

00:42:03.220 --> 00:42:04.517
of enjoying a meal.

00:42:07.558 --> 00:42:09.890
Foie gras with truffles,

00:42:09.960 --> 00:42:11.518
an ancient Earth delicacy.

00:42:11.595 --> 00:42:13.187
Chateau d'Yquem.

00:42:13.264 --> 00:42:15.027
According to
the culinary database,

00:42:15.099 --> 00:42:17.294
the ideal accompaniment.

00:42:17.368 --> 00:42:19.233
Not your usual fare.

00:42:19.303 --> 00:42:21.134
It's come to my attention

00:42:21.205 --> 00:42:24.834
that nutritional supplements
don't fully meet my needs.

00:42:24.909 --> 00:42:27.309
I see.

00:42:27.378 --> 00:42:30.040
I thought we could share
this experience.

00:42:30.114 --> 00:42:31.843
I'll describe the meal to you...

00:42:31.916 --> 00:42:34.714
the tastes, the sensations.

00:42:34.785 --> 00:42:37.151
Perhaps you can enjoy it
vicariously.

00:42:38.322 --> 00:42:39.812
What about the wine?

00:42:39.890 --> 00:42:42.950
It doesn't exactly agree
with you.

00:42:43.027 --> 00:42:46.258
If I become sick,
I won't have far to go.

00:42:50.200 --> 00:42:52.828
To shared experiences.

00:42:52.903 --> 00:42:54.461
Hear, hear.
